<title>BRAZIL: Soy shipping conditions at key Brazilian ports.</title>
<headline>Soy shipping conditions at key Brazilian ports.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian ports of Paranagua and Santos reported the following conditions for shipping soybeans and soy products:</p>
<p>PARANAGUA:</p>
<p>No data available due to a computer fault.</p>
<p>SANTOS:</p>
<p>Vessels: All vessels at public terminal paralyzed due to a strike by administrative portworkers. This includes the Powhatan which was loading 57,000 tonnes soymeal. One vessel waiting to dock to load soybeans, one vessel expected to load soybeans. At Cargill private terminal, Standard Endeavour continued loading 18,000 tonnes soymeal. No vessels waiting to dock, one vessel expected to load soymeal.</p>
<p>Road: no figures available due to strike.</p>
<p>Rail: no figures available.</p>
<p>Loading: no figures available.</p>
<p>Stocks: no figures available.</p>
<p>NOTE: All unloading at warehouses has stopped because of the labor</p>
<p>dispute.</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
